  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 10 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes, 12 of 12 including the two existing tests.\n\nIt runs these steps in order:\n- Replace `đ` and `Đ` with `d`.\n- Decompose accents and strip them.\n- Lowercase.\n- Turn each run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 into one hyphen.\n- Trim leading and trailing hyphens.\n- Cut to 50 characters, then trim any hyphen the cut left at the end.\n\nThe tests cover basic hyphenation, Vietnamese and other Latin accents, `đ`/`Đ`, collapsing runs, trimming, empty or symbol-only input (returns an empty string), truncation to 50, and no trailing hyphen after the cut.\n\nI haven't tried non-Latin scripts. Characters outside a-z and 0-9, such as CJK, become hyphens and are then trimmed, so a purely non-Latin input returns an empty string.",
